{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the smallest primitive root mod 11 is 2\n  how: (Z/11)* is cyclic of order phi = 10 = 2 * 5; g generates it iff g^(10/p) != 1 for each prime p | 10\n  phi(10) = 4 primitive roots: 2 6 7 8\n  check: the powers 2^0 .. 2^9 are 10 distinct units\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "primroot", "ucas": "primroot 11", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "primroot", "value": "2", "method": "(Z/11)* is cyclic of order phi = 10 = 2 * 5; g generates it iff g^(10/p) != 1 for each prime p | 10", "phi(10)": "4 primitive roots: 2 6 7 8", "headline": "the smallest primitive root mod 11 is 2"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the powers 2^0 .. 2^9 are 10 distinct units"}], "files": [], "text": "the smallest primitive root mod 11 is 2\n  how: (Z/11)* is cyclic of order phi = 10 = 2 * 5; g generates it iff g^(10/p) != 1 for each prime p | 10\n  phi(10) = 4 primitive roots: 2 6 7 8\n  check: the powers 2^0 .. 2^9 are 10 distinct units\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "yes: 1 is a primitive root mod 2 (its order is 1, phi(2) = 1)\n  how: (a primitive root has none of these equal to 1)\n  check: the powers 1^0 .. 1^0 are 1 distinct units\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "primroot", "ucas": "primroot 2 11", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "primroot", "primitive_root": true, "order": "1", "phi": "1", "method": "(a primitive root has none of these equal to 1)", "headline": "yes: 1 is a primitive root mod 2 (its order is 1, phi(2) = 1)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the powers 1^0 .. 1^0 are 1 distinct units"}], "files": [], "text": "yes: 1 is a primitive root mod 2 (its order is 1, phi(2) = 1)\n  how: (a primitive root has none of these equal to 1)\n  check: the powers 1^0 .. 1^0 are 1 distinct units\n"}, "isError": false}}
